  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** The AI infrastructure buildout is gaining tangible momentum. The company’s flagship Alabama data center campus is progressing on schedule, with Phase 1 nearing completion and Phase 2 well into planning. Early AI revenue is already flowing from the NeoCloudz GPU‑as‑a‑Service platform, which is live on NVIDIA B200/B300 hardware, and from an operational modular unit that has been serving AI workloads since May. The narrative reflects strong, sustained demand in the colocation and AI compute market, with no indication of slack or competitive displacement, positioning the business for a material revenue inflection as new capacity comes online.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership has executed crisply against its vertically integrated AI infrastructure vision. All major long‑lead equipment is secured, construction has transitioned to vertical erection, and the company remains debt‑free with ample liquidity—steps that de‑risk the buildout. By setting clear segment‑level targets for fiscal 2027 and already generating AI revenue ahead of the main campus launch, management is signaling operational confidence and establishing early credibility with the market. The team’s ability to bring capacity online without balance‑sheet strain reinforces a disciplined, growth‑oriented posture.",
